{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:34:34.165616Z","id":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1643},"end":{"line":1648},"content_hash":"d7d7999a2c1c93d287ddd23c909a4e8374ad6471e481c1f2e2c68db2057c588b"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697444Z","id":"0ec2218948961006563d459cb637b8f29888a013b1d02a2737ff98c8334ca7bf","body":{"detail":"Measured on a home seeded by main (schema 21, 300 artifacts, 11,664 comments, 1,585 versions), upgraded with bf1180d: 16,715 backfilled events, about 650 B each in audit_events with its indexes and 1.3 KB each in the journal. Neither is pruned by default (journal_retain_days 0, the table kept indefinitely), and an agent in a wait loop adds a tool.call (and under Claude Code a tool.call_id) every wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"fad347bfe0932bf3c8bfbb95022fe5089f50de6fe7c9d3a8672f5812ae9b436b"},"suggested_fix":"State the measured cost in the contract and README where [toolpath] is documented, and offer journal_retain_days in the upgrade note; consider whether wait_for_feedback calls need a tool.call each.","summary":"Disk use on upgrade is several times the history: a 9.2 MB perf-seed home grew to 20 MB of database plus a 22 MB journal","tags":["review","disk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697640Z","id":"1e79ad8b9a4a72940e4b2846bce0f2538ed389266b6e4e50225d8d7d7792ad31","body":{"detail":"Between the link and comment mode the shell and bridge make only GET requests plus PUT looked, seen, presence and the stream POST, all in UNAUDITED (crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs:719-764) and unchanged; web/shell differs from main only by type annotations (web/shell/src/api.ts), so the bundles are the same code. The only new background work during a sample is the journal appender's 1 s quiet tick, one indexed events_after read on a reader. A token publish now makes the CLI owner row, folded once by the first browser's token claim, which sample() does in its warm-up tab. Not measured on a quiet machine: the machine was loaded (load 7-15) and slept during this review.","kind":"comment","references":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","summary":"Traced the comment-ready path: nothing this branch records or changes runs on it","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.620876Z","id":"bc7fce33479e73db5bd96776ad9010791c1289b29c828dfbc9db17630154323b","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1719},"end":{"line":1724},"content_hash":"d7d7999a2c1c93d287ddd23c909a4e8374ad6471e481c1f2e2c68db2057c588b"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","supersedes":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259348Z","id":"501e7f1dda04d69e636620ec5ea2126629233cd1b0582a734a31c27579405ed3","body":{"detail":"Line 12 says the toolpath-audit design is on branch toolpath-audit, not yet merged; section 20 and M27 say it landed on main with migration 23.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ac3b777dfe6d4ae3767334718398649c37d62331fb2f48f454d098e8ea5b009f"},"suggested_fix":"Say it is on main (migration 23).","summary":"The header still calls toolpath-audit an unmerged branch","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:09:31.206624Z","id":"9673c3b260aae88688c8359ab0b17f22a06724482ce3d31497961b2f91444561","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e423bfb","summary":"Fixed: lines 11-12 now say the toolpath-audit design is on main since migration 23. Evidence: sed -n 11,12p of the spec at e423bfb prints 'Interacts with: `2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md` (on main since / migration 23; §20).'","supersedes":"501e7f1dda04d69e636620ec5ea2126629233cd1b0582a734a31c27579405ed3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.112813Z","id":"7f69c31973abd580fa5a24213f612f0daa7054b1ca9ed985f3a7c307397465c2","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1723},"end":{"line":1728},"content_hash":"8edc9b4bf3e025ca4a925a78d664702ff5637e4ad75054b1bfcb9c7c4158adf5"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","supersedes":"bc7fce33479e73db5bd96776ad9010791c1289b29c828dfbc9db17630154323b","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:41.798807Z","id":"7f264407e5224b2e8fe8598dde1ae0cef9763febf6649028caececaa8ef94563","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1725},"end":{"line":1730},"content_hash":"8edc9b4bf3e025ca4a925a78d664702ff5637e4ad75054b1bfcb9c7c4158adf5"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","supersedes":"7f69c31973abd580fa5a24213f612f0daa7054b1ca9ed985f3a7c307397465c2","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.887009Z","id":"4000ca14d6ad2b689b988bc7a4c84279aa590a81cad5f1bb3201dc72d0d1212b","body":{"detail":"In docs/verification.md §10.2 and §10.3 (2026-10-09, d436b13 against main 527db6c, shared machine at load 16-30), the branch's subdomain comment ready read 101, 98 and 100 ms in the quality gate's quick run (limit 94 ms, scale 1.09; all three attempts failed), 97 ms on one of three solo reruns (limit 86; its retry read 81), 86 ms in the full `just perf` run (limit 86), and 81 and 83 ms otherwise. Main's build read 81, 83, 82 and 80 ms in the same interleaved runs. Every other time-to-usable measure matched main. The gate retries absorbed it in the solo reruns but not in the gate run. Whether something the branch records on the path a page takes to comment-ready (a viewer row, an audit insert, the journal appender's read) costs this, or it is load, is not settled: measure web/perf/usable.perf.ts subdomain comment ready on a quiet machine, branch against main, before merging.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1726},"end":{"line":1731},"content_hash":"8edc9b4bf3e025ca4a925a78d664702ff5637e4ad75054b1bfcb9c7c4158adf5"},"summary":"Time to usable's subdomain comment ready runs over its limit on this branch now and then, never on main","supersedes":"7f264407e5224b2e8fe8598dde1ae0cef9763febf6649028caececaa8ef94563","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.822655Z","id":"44f6b8e8806731bd4803917abdb861d7db6d5a59c309ec5c49edeb12ec337c58","body":{"detail":"Spec §7.4 says a person narrows one agent and §3.4/O2 that an agent's person narrows its rights, but only Caller::PersonAgent requests are checked against rights (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs Agent<N>::from_request_parts); a token session (Caller::OwnerAgent) has none, and §21 trusts it at the owner's level. Storing a narrowing for it would show in People and change nothing, so Store::narrow_agent and Store::elevate_agent refuse it (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs live_grant_of, token_agent), and the spec text above says so. The owner's other machines (grants of the owner row) are narrowable. Options: keep the refusal (recommended: honest, no new enforcement path); or enforce rights on OwnerAgent requests that name a session, which every agent-route extractor would then check for the token too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":873},"end":{"line":876},"content_hash":"9e387e61b219775f2d3cfa838e0074deb8dc844ec8618bbe00281f0a3ee4565c"},"summary":"Narrowing and elevation are refused (400 token_agent) for this machine's agents, which act with the daemon token and are never rights-checked","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:7.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.919248Z","id":"bf4aa381d8a33c8c06bd7aef5c1fd018617ab617e3105caca7ba5c684d966a25","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"44f6b8e8806731bd4803917abdb861d7db6d5a59c309ec5c49edeb12ec337c58","summary":"Review of 0d857bda: recommend keeping the token_agent refusal. Only Caller::PersonAgent is rights-checked (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:949); §21 trusts a shell-capable owner agent at the owner's level, and such an agent also reaches the owner's sessionless /mcp and the CLI, so a stored narrowing on a token session would be a control People shows that binds nothing. The spec text at these lines was amended before this decision; if the owner rules for enforcement it must be reverted with it. The owner's other machines remain narrowable and elevatable (probe: 200 on PUT /api/people/me/grants/<own gid>/narrow, 400 not_narrower on a wider one-agent narrowing).","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.921296Z","id":"1675ca068fd3ea091747d3d66424f83b4557daa488181455d52cd3f8c33e0e0b","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator (2026-10-12): keep the token_agent refusal. Spec §21 trusts an owner agent with a shell at the owner's level, so a narrowing on a token session would bind nothing; the People UI must not offer narrowing or elevation for this machine's agents. The spec's revision history records the ruling (34c65221).","supersedes":"44f6b8e8806731bd4803917abdb861d7db6d5a59c309ec5c49edeb12ec337c58","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262588Z","id":"0165db1244045f5f5959de3e0e422f6f3bce7e80d1ba6a1ca9be7a7d5692dd0d","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 sends the session secret itself beside the signature, as Authorization carries the access token: a LAN sniffer who reads it cannot sign without the machine's key, and X-Clax-Session is already in the signed agent-header line. An HMAC keyed by the secret would keep it off the wire after issuance, but the daemon would have to hold the secret (or a key as good as it) to check one, where it now keeps only a hash that proves nothing, and the identity check would need the canonical string the verify layer builds. It also changes nothing against the trust limit (a process of the same OS user reads the credential file).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":853},"end":{"line":868},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"Prove an agent session with an HMAC over the canonical string instead of sending its secret in X-Clax-Session-Secret","tags":["revisit:TLS lands (O7) or a threat model needs session secrets kept off a sniffable LAN","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262766Z","id":"248d2a90dc442acce02c0452ef2d34aa7041f96f3ae8aed3a0d0389af0b38261","body":{"detail":"Would keep no secret on the daemon at all, but costs a second Ed25519 signature on every agent request, a second header in the canonical contract, and Ed25519 in every client (the shim, hooks, the CLI and Pi). Against agents that share one OS user it buys nothing over spec 2026-10-08 §6.8's secret: the private key would sit in the same 0600 file a sibling can read.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":853},"end":{"line":868},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"A key pair per agent session, each request signed a second time with it","tags":["revisit:agents of one machine run as separate OS users or in sandboxes that can keep a per-session key out of their siblings' reach","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262861Z","id":"07cd8db1fe3b8ce3c353dcd47745c725ba4daec0b9112c76108c00523b3f3f67","body":{"detail":"Rejected for spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a narrowing can take reads away too (an artifact left out of locations), and refusing only writes would leave those reads open to an agent that names no session. The intersection (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, sessionless_narrow) covers every action with §7.2's own operator. Its cost: a person's own remote CLI is held to their narrowest live agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":881},"end":{"line":898},"content_hash":"b621890be9fc455ac1daa44012321828f3bab906087ba00a39ab540289777fdd"},"summary":"Refuse a grant's session-less content writes while any of its sessions is narrowed, instead of narrowing session-less requests by every live narrowing","tags":["revisit:narrowings can no longer remove read actions, or people find the remote CLI held to an agent's narrowing surprising","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262939Z","id":"c4ff1520d54ead87bf7a54df0ab07f1c2a87ee8dc7aac95a8857d37309c89105","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":927},"end":{"line":936},"content_hash":"4221aa76a164b7570d373cad1fcc2eef3ff9840969777c3a8469e085cbac1dff"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638008Z","id":"cb02cfc4d630bb5dd2e3a70d0b95f669ad931c0b8e7f6590dca2f36960f9475d","body":{"detail":"Today a new session starts unnarrowed (§6.8 \"The trust limit\" says so for a hostile agent with a shell). Three benign paths reach it too: (1) a narrowed agent that runs another agent as a subprocess (claude -p, codex exec): the child registers its own session, unnarrowed (reproduced: a fresh registration on a machine with a narrowed session reads an artifact outside that narrowing, 200); (2) a narrowed agent whose session idles out (30 minutes for a remote session) or is ended: the shim re-registers on its next call with no narrowing (M2: narrowing ends with the session); (3) a harness restart. The session-less rule (§6.8 \"Rights without a session\") already accepts holding every request of the machine to its narrowest live agent.\n\nOptions: (a) keep as is and say in §6.8 and People that a narrowing lasts only for that session and does not bind agents it starts; (b) a grant's new session starts with the intersection of its live sessions' narrowings, the same rule as session-less requests (cheap: one query at insert; cost: a new terminal on a machine with a narrowed agent starts narrowed, and People must say why); (c) inherit only from the session matched by ancestor PID (narrower blast radius, but PID-based and weaker). Recommendation: (b), since it closes paths 1 and 3 for well-behaved agents at the cost the session-less rule already pays; path 2 needs the narrowing to survive an idle end, as watches do (§6.7), which is a separate call.","kind":"comment","references":"c4ff1520d54ead87bf7a54df0ab07f1c2a87ee8dc7aac95a8857d37309c89105","span":{"start":{"line":927},"end":{"line":935},"content_hash":"bd34295e0431452895728e302b392271f512a273822bfa1e3db145e9e31a5cd3"},"summary":"Owner decision: should a grant's new session start with the intersection of its machine's live narrowings, so that a narrowed agent cannot shed its narrowing by starting a new session?","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:6.8","review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:46.415504Z","id":"646b38730c1c577d85bec634edf6efe6e587dcec565844748af2e6a670bb9211","body":{"detail":"Rejected for spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a narrowing can take reads away too (an artifact left out of locations), and refusing only writes would leave those reads open to an agent that names no session. The intersection (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, sessionless_narrow) covers every action with §7.2's own operator. Its cost: a person's own remote CLI is held to their narrowest live agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":889},"end":{"line":906},"content_hash":"b621890be9fc455ac1daa44012321828f3bab906087ba00a39ab540289777fdd"},"summary":"Refuse a grant's session-less content writes while any of its sessions is narrowed, instead of narrowing session-less requests by every live narrowing","supersedes":"07cd8db1fe3b8ce3c353dcd47745c725ba4daec0b9112c76108c00523b3f3f67","tags":["revisit:narrowings can no longer remove read actions, or people find the remote CLI held to an agent's narrowing surprising","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:46.417174Z","id":"7684491e4bb6d85f8a50b10d7d4050fb3f825435a3b6e99c3c1744a7a3475c33","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":946},"end":{"line":955},"content_hash":"4221aa76a164b7570d373cad1fcc2eef3ff9840969777c3a8469e085cbac1dff"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","supersedes":"c4ff1520d54ead87bf7a54df0ab07f1c2a87ee8dc7aac95a8857d37309c89105","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:51:58.498103Z","id":"8c0e0dba0eb92133dffde6b66d4e074e6ec44569bb749e079b9cde51069b1c86","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":956},"end":{"line":965},"content_hash":"4221aa76a164b7570d373cad1fcc2eef3ff9840969777c3a8469e085cbac1dff"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","supersedes":"7684491e4bb6d85f8a50b10d7d4050fb3f825435a3b6e99c3c1744a7a3475c33","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.652440Z","id":"51dd259d7a552021c76dd949e1f7f26c28e46b0ce6326188376db95563d55cc2","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1426},"end":{"line":1451},"content_hash":"7d0cf372583d8173105a6d1a5b39f8862968032f98d05d3af52fdab2a20e6e68"},"summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-13): \"Only about their content\". Who approves first: the owner's browser learns it for every person; a connected person P for P's own agents whatever the authors, and for another person's agents (the owner's included) only about content P wrote (P's comments, or a page P published), never another person's approval of a third author; LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents get 403, and the shell does not ask. Sections 10 and 18 amended to match.","tags":["status:decided","decision","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884502Z","id":"fc36a9cf936048731293341c1bd6c28480eeb5be04c2a02c9a58e6a7c7a7f8ad","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1451},"end":{"line":1467},"content_hash":"a2e2abbe169d17bd17494f287e3ab24dc9d84fae3bafd87a6186478599943027"},"summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-14): \"Declined by Mia\" for those concerned. After a decline, the owner, the decliner and the thread's authors read the thread as declined by that person; everyone else reads the plain delivery state (seen by the agent once the agent takes). Section 10 defines the three readings, including a later approval or revocation, a new comment by the same author, a handoff and the session ending.","tags":["status:decided","decision","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884651Z","id":"c56b670b9af3ba1be9e35f8f66b9abda4aebc77052c9f57d080615d7ca90adf9","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1468},"end":{"line":1488},"content_hash":"ebc297c4e087d916d496efaff1afe842b7160d85fb926c9692fff378cf26d24c"},"summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-14): plain \"sent\" for visitors. LAN viewers, anonymous views and events never read withheld, waiting for approval or declined; they read sent until delivery, and a decision publishes no event they hear. Connected people keep the 'Only about their content' rule. And: \"No\" for the owner's agents: agents never read an approver, the owner's included; withheld reads 'waiting for approval' with no name.","tags":["status:decided","decision","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884727Z","id":"1d96024914d43da73b831c839c53a76ee2ee86c1909963ffcbb048c1c7fb6358","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1749},"end":{"line":1751},"content_hash":"e0487bc4aa7928d12581a132cb577cbb4cf7f5ee0bbcc323d4fd9c1c0dac4390"},"summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-14): threads show the withheld and declined states only as section 10 says who reads them (\"Declined by Mia\" for those concerned; plain \"sent\" for visitors).","tags":["status:decided","decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884796Z","id":"502a40232e32c47fc8bf0a48d42d63f8aa1f3b61cf2a4600cdd0233d80de4115","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1765},"end":{"line":1765},"content_hash":"7c5624f870199f767d90a32510cf5965e9c5f852d7f3558813ee0fc8c3e86d27"},"summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-14): \"No\" for the owner's agents (no approver, ever), plain \"sent\" for visitors (LAN viewers read plain delivery states), and connected people keep 'Only about their content' for whose approval a thread waits for.","tags":["status:decided","decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.872449Z","id":"f9af22e71086a83bc9714e54c4440cf6c9d8d44ac9157cc186b98cba861e72d7","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 sends the session secret itself beside the signature, as Authorization carries the access token: a LAN sniffer who reads it cannot sign without the machine's key, and X-Clax-Session is already in the signed agent-header line. An HMAC keyed by the secret would keep it off the wire after issuance, but the daemon would have to hold the secret (or a key as good as it) to check one, where it now keeps only a hash that proves nothing, and the identity check would need the canonical string the verify layer builds. It also changes nothing against the trust limit (a process of the same OS user reads the credential file).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":876},"end":{"line":891},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"Prove an agent session with an HMAC over the canonical string instead of sending its secret in X-Clax-Session-Secret","supersedes":"0165db1244045f5f5959de3e0e422f6f3bce7e80d1ba6a1ca9be7a7d5692dd0d","tags":["revisit:TLS lands (O7) or a threat model needs session secrets kept off a sniffable LAN","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.873498Z","id":"3fd670924907fd2271a83dee38977186b4dce691a3dd62fedc351546d52c46ac","body":{"detail":"Would keep no secret on the daemon at all, but costs a second Ed25519 signature on every agent request, a second header in the canonical contract, and Ed25519 in every client (the shim, hooks, the CLI and Pi). Against agents that share one OS user it buys nothing over spec 2026-10-08 §6.8's secret: the private key would sit in the same 0600 file a sibling can read.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":876},"end":{"line":891},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"A key pair per agent session, each request signed a second time with it","supersedes":"248d2a90dc442acce02c0452ef2d34aa7041f96f3ae8aed3a0d0389af0b38261","tags":["revisit:agents of one machine run as separate OS users or in sandboxes that can keep a per-session key out of their siblings' reach","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.874395Z","id":"c978c4691209e93ad483b5d6fc62914fe1dccb4ce0a871c04c2e7f04ecd7dcf5","body":{"detail":"Rejected for spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a narrowing can take reads away too (an artifact left out of locations), and refusing only writes would leave those reads open to an agent that names no session. The intersection (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, sessionless_narrow) covers every action with §7.2's own operator. Its cost: a person's own remote CLI is held to their narrowest live agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":912},"end":{"line":929},"content_hash":"b621890be9fc455ac1daa44012321828f3bab906087ba00a39ab540289777fdd"},"summary":"Refuse a grant's session-less content writes while any of its sessions is narrowed, instead of narrowing session-less requests by every live narrowing","supersedes":"646b38730c1c577d85bec634edf6efe6e587dcec565844748af2e6a670bb9211","tags":["revisit:narrowings can no longer remove read actions, or people find the remote CLI held to an agent's narrowing surprising","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.875256Z","id":"baa1c5199f1567359fdef85ed0eca8298b930bc930365fb3665142a78340a2c5","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":979},"end":{"line":987},"content_hash":"bd34295e0431452895728e302b392271f512a273822bfa1e3db145e9e31a5cd3"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","supersedes":"8c0e0dba0eb92133dffde6b66d4e074e6ec44569bb749e079b9cde51069b1c86","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.876065Z","id":"ff873cf298ff3aa93118afc4279c2332b6f365b12aeccefc77e1bb6a8d79531e","body":{"detail":"The owner's words: \"Agents can have the max permissions equal to that of their \"owner\", that owner can choose what permissions any given agent has below that bound, and an agent can be given more permission than it's \"owner\" by the creator of a given artifact, etc.\" and \"The creator of an artifact is its defacto owner and the one who has responsibility for delegation\". Recorded in the spec as decision O11: effective rights are (person ∩ grant.narrow ∩ session.narrow) ∪ one elevation per granter; the install owner elevates anywhere, an artifact's creator only on artifacts they created and only within their own rights there (lines 1011-1043; who may change what: §7.4).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1011},"end":{"line":1043},"content_hash":"de4041d4105948e559176c926b27d992461f296683e067d9241cf032fe83986d"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): an artifact's creator delegates; an agent may be given more than its person by the creator of an artifact","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:27.876139Z","id":"34de4da0872483919f328d254513db14dace443dc85e4a5be84125b085f50ea7","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1451},"end":{"line":1461},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:47.075737Z","id":"e0cd35f1f488f76d91b2f650823e3aec69c0b21559e067f244c61c981a0bbef7","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1455},"end":{"line":1465},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","supersedes":"34de4da0872483919f328d254513db14dace443dc85e4a5be84125b085f50ea7","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:34.936784Z","id":"296679910d29d571930f97ac23ebba5c370077fe5494bef22178e4981b87a61d","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question in reply cb02cfc4 (option (b), a new session starting with the intersection of its machine's live narrowings, was not taken): \"Starts at the bound\". A fresh agent session starts at its person's rights intersected with its grant's narrowing; it inherits no other session's narrowing. Spec section 6.8 now says so in its own bullet (lines 988-993) and decision O11 names it; the session-less rule (every live narrowing binds a request naming no session) is unchanged. Implemented as it already was: crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs grant_caller_in reads only the named session's narrowing and elevations.","kind":"comment","references":"baa1c5199f1567359fdef85ed0eca8298b930bc930365fb3665142a78340a2c5","span":{"start":{"line":988},"end":{"line":993},"content_hash":"6d2de395300aac76716f7ed77ada6020b9be160a12ce0275fe0585f95f2314a8"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Starts at the bound\": a new session starts at its person's rights within its machine's narrowing and inherits no other session's narrowing","tags":["status:decided","spec:6.8","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835853Z","id":"285736808de34db45f7fee0930d70498e738212c208ff886fdcf68b065a46c7f","body":{"detail":"The 'An elevation also ends when its granter's rights to give it end' paragraph sits between steps 4 and 5 of the numbered list of what a session's end does, so it reads as one of those steps and the list restarts at 5. Move it after step 7. It also omits what the store does when the granter's rights are reduced (the raise is bounded at every check and silently applies again when the owner restores the rights; nothing is recorded) and when the granter stops being a connected person without revocation (release_unconnected, crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs): the row stays, inert. Say both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1643},"end":{"line":1647},"content_hash":"087fb91aa6b790f3e441d99b04c56a1c130e086d734d5653ff9fadb21b0cbcdc"},"summary":"§14's paragraph on elevations ending splits the session-end steps: steps 5-7 now follow it as a separate list","tags":["review","spec","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835948Z","id":"91e64b8f03cccf15a0c3b2bfaa75a8a37ec0a050042afce719f73638c4615475","body":{"detail":"As specified (§3.4, §7.2), only the granter or the agent's end removes a creator's raise; the agent's person cannot remove it, and narrowing does not bound it ('∪ comes after ∩'), so Mia, who narrowed her agent to clax:reader, still has an agent that may publish and delete Sam's artifact until she ends it. The owner can only demote or revoke Sam, not remove his raise of one agent. O11 says a creator 'can give' an agent more; it does not say the agent's person cannot decline. Options: (A) as now; (B) the agent's person may remove any raise of their own agent, and the owner any raise (recommended: the person answers for what their agent does, and the owner bounds everyone; the creator can raise again and the person sees who raised what); (C) B plus the person's narrowing also bounds raises (would make a narrowed agent unraisable).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1035},"end":{"line":1038},"content_hash":"32da5c85d735e4fe121d6f0f4ed58822d858bc11b6d3511b815d42844649d013"},"summary":"Question for the owner: may an agent's own person (and the owner) remove an artifact creator's raise of that agent?","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.272611Z","id":"995f6203d3798064cec6fa3eaea41d28cbbdcf60ded6247adf358955cc65a726","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 sends the session secret itself beside the signature, as Authorization carries the access token: a LAN sniffer who reads it cannot sign without the machine's key, and X-Clax-Session is already in the signed agent-header line. An HMAC keyed by the secret would keep it off the wire after issuance, but the daemon would have to hold the secret (or a key as good as it) to check one, where it now keeps only a hash that proves nothing, and the identity check would need the canonical string the verify layer builds. It also changes nothing against the trust limit (a process of the same OS user reads the credential file).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":878},"end":{"line":893},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"Prove an agent session with an HMAC over the canonical string instead of sending its secret in X-Clax-Session-Secret","supersedes":"f9af22e71086a83bc9714e54c4440cf6c9d8d44ac9157cc186b98cba861e72d7","tags":["revisit:TLS lands (O7) or a threat model needs session secrets kept off a sniffable LAN","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.276358Z","id":"9366858c30103b3940cb203f09e48350487f2599756e0825b6556f22f4b4d73d","body":{"detail":"Would keep no secret on the daemon at all, but costs a second Ed25519 signature on every agent request, a second header in the canonical contract, and Ed25519 in every client (the shim, hooks, the CLI and Pi). Against agents that share one OS user it buys nothing over spec 2026-10-08 §6.8's secret: the private key would sit in the same 0600 file a sibling can read.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":878},"end":{"line":893},"content_hash":"c3b7feb62f8177fe9d7c166e8e369cc4634f394e06332667985c690d562b48b4"},"summary":"A key pair per agent session, each request signed a second time with it","supersedes":"3fd670924907fd2271a83dee38977186b4dce691a3dd62fedc351546d52c46ac","tags":["revisit:agents of one machine run as separate OS users or in sandboxes that can keep a per-session key out of their siblings' reach","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.278149Z","id":"f000550e81c95841a68fca20dd293782ec3d1d6f4c11294045a23f035c5ba5d9","body":{"detail":"Rejected for spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a narrowing can take reads away too (an artifact left out of locations), and refusing only writes would leave those reads open to an agent that names no session. The intersection (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, sessionless_narrow) covers every action with §7.2's own operator. Its cost: a person's own remote CLI is held to their narrowest live agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":914},"end":{"line":931},"content_hash":"b621890be9fc455ac1daa44012321828f3bab906087ba00a39ab540289777fdd"},"summary":"Refuse a grant's session-less content writes while any of its sessions is narrowed, instead of narrowing session-less requests by every live narrowing","supersedes":"c978c4691209e93ad483b5d6fc62914fe1dccb4ce0a871c04c2e7f04ecd7dcf5","tags":["revisit:narrowings can no longer remove read actions, or people find the remote CLI held to an agent's narrowing surprising","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.279211Z","id":"ef4c25c447df2b3419b7cb386520bfe18eda112fb93e829929651601b6c065ae","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":981},"end":{"line":989},"content_hash":"bd34295e0431452895728e302b392271f512a273822bfa1e3db145e9e31a5cd3"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","supersedes":"baa1c5199f1567359fdef85ed0eca8298b930bc930365fb3665142a78340a2c5","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.280209Z","id":"6085ec8193f470765ee31d4833b5e63496d096297f6c3f40ad23d8e90104d7aa","body":{"detail":"The owner's words: \"Agents can have the max permissions equal to that of their \"owner\", that owner can choose what permissions any given agent has below that bound, and an agent can be given more permission than it's \"owner\" by the creator of a given artifact, etc.\" and \"The creator of an artifact is its defacto owner and the one who has responsibility for delegation\". Recorded in the spec as decision O11: effective rights are (person ∩ grant.narrow ∩ session.narrow) ∪ one elevation per granter; the install owner elevates anywhere, an artifact's creator only on artifacts they created and only within their own rights there (lines 1011-1043; who may change what: §7.4).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1013},"end":{"line":1045},"content_hash":"de4041d4105948e559176c926b27d992461f296683e067d9241cf032fe83986d"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): an artifact's creator delegates; an agent may be given more than its person by the creator of an artifact","supersedes":"ff873cf298ff3aa93118afc4279c2332b6f365b12aeccefc77e1bb6a8d79531e","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.281222Z","id":"6c8489b017cc61b9c38c604b8e95c9d76cb7301fbcda50c845e8cf4f21491d55","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1463},"end":{"line":1473},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","supersedes":"e0cd35f1f488f76d91b2f650823e3aec69c0b21559e067f244c61c981a0bbef7","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:18:00.282238Z","id":"84730f9e888f36e387e6f47833ba73b90bc8b751545e36719897da66360a30b5","body":{"detail":"As specified (§3.4, §7.2), only the granter or the agent's end removes a creator's raise; the agent's person cannot remove it, and narrowing does not bound it ('∪ comes after ∩'), so Mia, who narrowed her agent to clax:reader, still has an agent that may publish and delete Sam's artifact until she ends it. The owner can only demote or revoke Sam, not remove his raise of one agent. O11 says a creator 'can give' an agent more; it does not say the agent's person cannot decline. Options: (A) as now; (B) the agent's person may remove any raise of their own agent, and the owner any raise (recommended: the person answers for what their agent does, and the owner bounds everyone; the creator can raise again and the person sees who raised what); (C) B plus the person's narrowing also bounds raises (would make a narrowed agent unraisable).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1037},"end":{"line":1040},"content_hash":"32da5c85d735e4fe121d6f0f4ed58822d858bc11b6d3511b815d42844649d013"},"summary":"Question for the owner: may an agent's own person (and the owner) remove an artifact creator's raise of that agent?","supersedes":"91e64b8f03cccf15a0c3b2bfaa75a8a37ec0a050042afce719f73638c4615475","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.135292Z","id":"11e647b235646e7cbdac2cbe0d6b5720f5adebb2e45d20552eb00d091276f179","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e711084d","summary":"Fixed: §14's session-end steps 1-7 are one list again; the ways a raise ends follow it as their own paragraph and list (session end, removal, person_revoked, person_released, viewer_folded, artifact_deleted for soft and outright deletes), with reduced creator rights bounding the raise at each check without deleting it. The code drops on release, fold and outright delete since 7329a263 (store::elevations::tests::hard_deletes_releases_and_folds_drop_the_raises_left_behind passes; no-release-drop and no-fold-drop mutations fail it).","supersedes":"285736808de34db45f7fee0930d70498e738212c208ff886fdcf68b065a46c7f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:57:48.758097Z","id":"feda6d0cb6717975b38f8d7f370b898a21b26d57e2da0f1c990476d9d2922032","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1490},"end":{"line":1500},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","supersedes":"6c8489b017cc61b9c38c604b8e95c9d76cb7301fbcda50c845e8cf4f21491d55","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:57:48.761860Z","id":"c3274c3c99805c28bdb00cc82ec7656ef89bd192082ca8e5a2fbcdf8a3fc0746","body":{"detail":"The owner's words: \"Agents can have the max permissions equal to that of their \"owner\", that owner can choose what permissions any given agent has below that bound, and an agent can be given more permission than it's \"owner\" by the creator of a given artifact, etc.\" and \"The creator of an artifact is its defacto owner and the one who has responsibility for delegation\". Recorded in the spec as decision O11: effective rights are (person ∩ grant.narrow ∩ session.narrow) ∪ one elevation per granter; the install owner elevates anywhere, an artifact's creator only on artifacts they created and only within their own rights there (lines 1011-1043; who may change what: §7.4).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1013},"end":{"line":1067},"content_hash":"ad08a564604208748dce6c5aebb44dad020352420380e0bb9fa454c6246ef5ac"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): an artifact's creator delegates; an agent may be given more than its person by the creator of an artifact","supersedes":"6085ec8193f470765ee31d4833b5e63496d096297f6c3f40ad23d8e90104d7aa","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:57:48.764319Z","id":"f53399b5bf768fcb5f51ee045b3bc026b1238fc0fe7c2c865ef6e59ceafed70c","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Narrowing caps raises\": the agent's person's narrowing (and the grant narrowing) is the last word for that agent. Stated in §7.2 as cap(): every raise loses each action a narrowing turns off (one what it narrows allows somewhere and it allows nowhere), and a lowered db level lowers the raise's; by action and level, not location, because a narrowing is stated within the person's rights, whose locations a raise exists to exceed. Implemented by rights::cap_raise in rights::effective (crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1041},"end":{"line":1058},"content_hash":"b19fb35ea2487eae6aa3ea7cdc96b624e862b5e954120938617f72ed0ecb8eb2"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Narrowing caps raises\"","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:57:48.764776Z","id":"a2e6bc19df6455cfdb1429327ab3801a0657c0b99e20093a7850d3e992ce56ec","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Both may remove\": the agent's own person and the install owner may each remove any creator's raise on that agent; the granter can raise again, and the person or owner can remove it again. Stated in §7.2, §7.4 (DELETE ?granter=), §14 and §18; replaces the interpretation that a raise was its granter's alone to remove.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1090},"end":{"line":1096},"content_hash":"33da3f4974c8921cbc9a99987b55def38ce33dbf99fb6fdc7528759382ff125b"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Both may remove\"","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.4","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:13:53.802954Z","id":"b5bd20bb5d4ff65f404fe4c59e64ba0db4436445e22b46f6da5e0becd3e429c8","body":{"detail":"The owner's selections, verbatim: \"Both may remove\": the agent's own person and the install owner may each remove any creator's raise on that agent; the granter can raise again, and the person or owner can remove it again. \"Narrowing caps raises\": the agent's person's narrowing (and the grant narrowing) is the last word for that agent. Spec §7.2 (cap), §7.4 (DELETE ?granter=), §3.4, §14, §17, §18, M6 and the O11 row state both.","kind":"comment","references":"84730f9e888f36e387e6f47833ba73b90bc8b751545e36719897da66360a30b5","summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Both may remove\" and \"Narrowing caps raises\"","tags":["status:decided","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:13:53.803051Z","id":"b306c3fe755d40e0d6051554343f70d3262ea7d577ae5759cac140baa1758760","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21eb815c","summary":"Answered by the owner (option B, and narrowing caps raises) and implemented: 21eb815c (DELETE /api/agents/<handle>/elevate?granter= for the agent's person and the owner; rights::cap_raise in rights::effective), 81356182 (spec), and the People Remove controls and narrowing notes. Evidence: cargo nextest run --workspace passes (2201), including api_people::the_agents_person_and_the_owner_remove_a_creators_raise_and_no_one_else (Mia and the owner remove Sam's raise, audited removed_by_person with Mia as actor and removed_by_owner; Lee gets 404 not_raised, nothing recorded) and api_people::a_persons_narrowing_caps_a_creators_raise (Mia's read-only narrowing stops her raised agent publishing Sam's Notes; removing the narrowing brings it back); rights::tests::a_narrowing_caps_raises_by_action_and_level; mutations removing the cap, the level cap, the base check, the person's removal, or opening removal to anyone each fail a test.","supersedes":"84730f9e888f36e387e6f47833ba73b90bc8b751545e36719897da66360a30b5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.398373Z","id":"72e8a72b26693119c80c0bddb343f1d0a7d10814e6083fdee0ddb12d0b60050f","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1495},"end":{"line":1505},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","supersedes":"feda6d0cb6717975b38f8d7f370b898a21b26d57e2da0f1c990476d9d2922032","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.402770Z","id":"fee293a4496b5f77d5bb2ef9df69792fff5a93a38828b5f2bccdc88b1807a8d5","body":{"detail":"The owner's words: \"Agents can have the max permissions equal to that of their \"owner\", that owner can choose what permissions any given agent has below that bound, and an agent can be given more permission than it's \"owner\" by the creator of a given artifact, etc.\" and \"The creator of an artifact is its defacto owner and the one who has responsibility for delegation\". Recorded in the spec as decision O11: effective rights are (person ∩ grant.narrow ∩ session.narrow) ∪ one elevation per granter; the install owner elevates anywhere, an artifact's creator only on artifacts they created and only within their own rights there (lines 1011-1043; who may change what: §7.4).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1013},"end":{"line":1071},"content_hash":"c3373466c90fc58114d8e639d03b01fd0e65ad9c3e0a67bc8a24813486648921"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): an artifact's creator delegates; an agent may be given more than its person by the creator of an artifact","supersedes":"c3274c3c99805c28bdb00cc82ec7656ef89bd192082ca8e5a2fbcdf8a3fc0746","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.405514Z","id":"2cbf83d7ac554379f2f9b864f0b38fc425f9fc46ceadf6b1056e67469573727a","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Narrowing caps raises\": the agent's person's narrowing (and the grant narrowing) is the last word for that agent. Stated in §7.2 as cap(): every raise loses each action a narrowing turns off (one what it narrows allows somewhere and it allows nowhere), and a lowered db level lowers the raise's; by action and level, not location, because a narrowing is stated within the person's rights, whose locations a raise exists to exceed. Implemented by rights::cap_raise in rights::effective (crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1041},"end":{"line":1061},"content_hash":"bc497ccf770f8d46261d1c9f2b4a21b37d2aae45db6c15e826d7e39e07f1b4f9"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Narrowing caps raises\"","supersedes":"f53399b5bf768fcb5f51ee045b3bc026b1238fc0fe7c2c865ef6e59ceafed70c","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.407342Z","id":"5465a0243b052892bed05a7d52a328d9faf37bbb9e9aacc4f30f7f93433a454f","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Both may remove\": the agent's own person and the install owner may each remove any creator's raise on that agent; the granter can raise again, and the person or owner can remove it again. Stated in §7.2, §7.4 (DELETE ?granter=), §14 and §18; replaces the interpretation that a raise was its granter's alone to remove.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1094},"end":{"line":1102},"content_hash":"d14bea70ad80c56928fef5dd863aab9ecce04638a0bba1a8719bcba0b1354ec5"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): \"Both may remove\"","supersedes":"a2e6bc19df6455cfdb1429327ab3801a0657c0b99e20093a7850d3e992ce56ec","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.4","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.410037Z","id":"3659450ff1022a06048f2424ab15677c690f9b232c9f9e08ab5c3b8231a8530e","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Remove is enough\": narrowing caps raises only for actions the person holds; for anything else they use Remove; People's narrowing panel stays as it is. This confirms rights::cap_raise as built (crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs), stated in §7.2.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1041},"end":{"line":1061},"content_hash":"bc497ccf770f8d46261d1c9f2b4a21b37d2aae45db6c15e826d7e39e07f1b4f9"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): \"Remove is enough\"","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.410333Z","id":"5d80366c333ba5fca1e8f2eec028edf60af6f8aa29a5083892d0b38e7b5f395b","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Yes\": a person may also remove a raise the install owner gave their agent. Confirms what DELETE /api/agents/<handle>/elevate?granter=owner already does for the agent's person (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs unelevate_agent); stated in §7.2 and §7.4.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1062},"end":{"line":1066},"content_hash":"bef8bff51138bef77c171b7bb8774b5a9d1326d1e10113528989035f0cd030d1"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): \"Yes\", a person may remove a raise the install owner gave their agent","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.4","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.410667Z","id":"9717385be6fab407f9a3d9797095d1774b0037727d03ba554f5a29ca9710a032","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Yes\": a person may also remove a raise the install owner gave their agent. §7.4's DELETE ?granter=owner from the agent's person.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1094},"end":{"line":1102},"content_hash":"d14bea70ad80c56928fef5dd863aab9ecce04638a0bba1a8719bcba0b1354ec5"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): \"Yes\", the agent's person removes the owner's raise too","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.4","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T20:54:39.768301Z","id":"5bd44fa171c711e40c2c629894884df5f1411ad3e03c0be9952ee71f53b33294","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer to the question of record 9f714fe5 (web/shell/src/people/PersonCard.svelte) was \"Your content only\": on a person's card the install owner also sees that person's live approvals whose author is the owner (approvals covering the owner's content); a person's approvals of others' content stay private to them. Recorded in the spec as decision O12, here in §9.5, and in §17 and §18.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1502},"end":{"line":1512},"content_hash":"316dfaafd68de7d72388900b58912ec1b24fc29db0f49a37bae9b0d00b10217c"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): approvals in both directions on People, \"Your content only\"","supersedes":"72e8a72b26693119c80c0bddb343f1d0a7d10814e6083fdee0ddb12d0b60050f","tags":["status:decided","spec:9.5","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.523483Z","id":"274fe4c4d7c3c281a3546ade1790def39a02320c4e23b2227c77b652e42ee0da","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 O10 and §6.8: every agent on a connected machine runs as the same OS user, so the machine's key (remote.key) and every file in <home>/remote-sessions/ are readable by all of them, and a new registration starts from the machine's rights. Per-agent narrowing and elevation hold against mistakes and well-behaved agents (pinned by api_people::a_sibling_cannot_act_as_an_elevated_session_without_its_secret and a_narrowed_agent_cannot_write_by_naming_no_session); the machine, meaning its OS user, is the hard boundary, which §21, §25 and People's MACHINE_BOUNDARY line say. Narrowing the machine binds every agent of it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":989},"end":{"line":997},"content_hash":"bd34295e0431452895728e302b392271f512a273822bfa1e3db145e9e31a5cd3"},"summary":"Per-agent credentials do not stop a hostile agent with a shell: it can read its siblings' session credentials or register a fresh, unnarrowed session with the machine's key","supersedes":"ef4c25c447df2b3419b7cb386520bfe18eda112fb93e829929651601b6c065ae","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.525270Z","id":"b404869e45897e4cf813726e968f9ee2325cab7669c2d4bd8d461df6266c6c6f","body":{"detail":"The owner's words: \"Agents can have the max permissions equal to that of their \"owner\", that owner can choose what permissions any given agent has below that bound, and an agent can be given more permission than it's \"owner\" by the creator of a given artifact, etc.\" and \"The creator of an artifact is its defacto owner and the one who has responsibility for delegation\". Recorded in the spec as decision O11: effective rights are (person ∩ grant.narrow ∩ session.narrow) ∪ one elevation per granter; the install owner elevates anywhere, an artifact's creator only on artifacts they created and only within their own rights there (lines 1011-1043; who may change what: §7.4).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1021},"end":{"line":1079},"content_hash":"c3373466c90fc58114d8e639d03b01fd0e65ad9c3e0a67bc8a24813486648921"},"summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-13): an artifact's creator delegates; an agent may be given more than its person by the creator of an artifact","supersedes":"fee293a4496b5f77d5bb2ef9df69792fff5a93a38828b5f2bccdc88b1807a8d5","tags":["status:decided","spec:7.2","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
